.claude/settings.local.json
backend/.env
# Both spellings: `python -m venv .venv` is the common one and was missing,
# so a whole interpreter's worth of site-packages was one `git add -A` away
# from the history.
backend/venv/
backend/.venv/
venv/
.venv/
# FPL data snapshots live in a sibling data/ folder at the repo root. The
# archived training files plus a pinned live snapshot (bootstrap_static.json /
# fixtures.json) are tracked so the deterministic golden tests reproduce for
# everyone - ensure_data_fetched only fetches when these are missing, so the
# committed copies win. Generated CSVs stay ignored.
data/*
!data/bootstrap_static_2025_26_final.json
!data/fixtures_2025_26_final.json
# Every season's gameweek history, not just the archived one: the model
# blends the season being played into the archive as results accrue, and it
# reads that from here whenever there is no database (see
# backend/tools/build_gw_history.py). A per-season line would mean the blend
# silently stays switched off every August until someone remembered.
!data/gw_history_*.csv
!data/bootstrap_static.json
!data/fixtures.json
# The public track record. Tracked for the same reason as the snapshots above:
# /api/accuracy has a golden, and a golden computed from an untracked file is
# not reproducible - CI would either regrade over the network or diff against
# grades it has no way to produce. The refresh workflow rebuilds and commits
# this alongside the snapshots.
!data/accuracy.json
# The model's own season, replayed under the game's rules (see /accuracy).
# Tracked for the same reason as accuracy.json: it is public evidence, it is
# rebuilt by the refresh workflow after each gameweek, and rebuilding it on a
# page load would mean an integer program per gameweek plus a binary search
# through ten million league entries.
!data/season_run.json
# Projections frozen before each deadline. These are the evidence behind the
# accuracy page's pre-commitment claim, so they are tracked by pattern rather
# than by gameweek - a freeze that failed to get committed because nobody
# added a line for GW17 would silently downgrade that week to a reconstruction.
!data/projections/
!data/projections/*.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc

frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.next/
